there's a renewed interest in the committees and working

01:25:17.640 --> 01:25:19.000
groups. So, you know, again, I would

01:25:19.000 --> 01:25:22.480
just encourage anybody who wants to participate to reach out

01:25:23.120 --> 01:25:29.640
civil comps at fai.org, civil under score comps or to me or to

01:25:29.640 --> 01:25:32.480
Goran or you know, anybody that they know on the Bureau or their

01:25:32.480 --> 01:25:35.240
delegate. And we would, we would love to,

01:25:35.280 --> 01:25:36.800
we would love to have their contributions.

01:25:37.800 --> 01:25:40.640
I think most importantly, what I really would like to point out,

01:25:40.640 --> 01:25:43.920
not just to to both of you, but to the audiences as well as that

01:25:44.400 --> 01:25:47.760
as long as we have people at the top who are willing to take

01:25:47.760 --> 01:25:51.680
questions as transparently as you guys do, I don't think there

01:25:51.680 --> 01:25:53.880
should be anything to worry about because I think it was, it

01:25:53.880 --> 01:25:56.800
was important generally in the parallel learning community that

01:25:56.800 --> 01:25:59.720
information like this should be unfiltered, come out as

01:25:59.720 --> 01:26:03.040
unfiltered as possible. I think we have managed to do

01:26:03.040 --> 01:26:05.400
that task today. So thank you guys.

01:26:05.400 --> 01:26:08.080
It's been, it's been an honor. Try to do it.
